@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  *,
  *::before,
  *::after {
    animation-duration: 0.01ms !important;
    animation-iteration-count: 1 !important;
    transition-duration: 0.01ms !important;
  }
}

content.text:
Now main.ts + UI class. This is the biggest integration. Let's design in detail.

Main.ts responsibilities:
- import three, font CSS, style.
- await document.fonts.ready maybe timeout.
- Create BoardScene.
- Create app instance.

GameApp fields:
```ts
private scene: BoardScene
private game: MilestoneGame | null
private modalRoot: HTMLElement
private toastEl...
private mode
private turnToken = 0
private busy = false
private setup: PlayerSetup[] = default
private lastSetup: PlayerSetup[] | null
private selectedTile: number|null
private soundOn = localStorage?
private eventTimer
private modalLocked = false
private aiTimer: number | null
private rules/back target
```

DOM refs.

Initialization:
```ts
constructor():
 scene = new BoardScene(sceneEl);
 scene.onTileClick = idx => this.inspectTile(idx)
 load settings
 setupTitle()
 showTitle()
 renderTopbarButtons()
 scene preview
 // demo state
```
Preview: create demo game with 4 players (careers, colors), set some owners/levels, maybe player positions. But `MilestoneGame.newGame` kicks log etc. Use state. Pawns at start; place at chosen tiles. Set `demo.state.players[i].tile = [0,11,20,29][i]`; `properties` owners: indexes 1,4,13,20,28 with levels 1-3; sync. Also show dice values 3/4. `scene.showDice([3,4])`.
Set active player 0.

But then starting a new game calls scene.setPlayers(new players) and sync. Good.

Title screen HTML:
```
<section class title-screen ...>
 <div class title-copy>
  <div eyebrow>3D BOARD GAME • OFFLINE</div>
  <h1>MILE<span>STONE</span></h1>
  <div class title-sub>Roll · Build · Live</div>
  <p class title-desc>...</p>
  <div class title-actions>
    <button id=btn-new class=btn btn-primary>New Game icon</button>
    <button id=btn-continue ... hidden>Continue Story</button>
    <button id=btn-rules class="btn btn-ghost">How to Play</button>
  </div>
  <div class title-meta>2–4 players · Pass & play or vs. AI · No internet needed</div>
 </div>
 <div class title-foot>v1.0.0 · Made for Android</div>
</section>
```
Bind buttons each render (title screen innerHTML replaced). Add sound icon to title actions? Topbar hidden on title. Add small sound toggle in title meta row maybe. Could show topbar on title with only sound? CSS `.is-title .topbar` hidden. Add a round icon button absolutely placed top-right title: "sound". Include in title-screen markup `button.title-sound`. Bind.

Title screen could show "Continue Story" only if valid save. Load save state lazily. If saved, display. Also show "Latest: ..." maybe not.

`showTitle()`:
- app.className = 'app is-title'
- scene.stopCelebrate; scene.setSelectedTile(null); scene.showPreview? Need restore demo players and state. Use `showPreview()`.
- hide modals; empty modal.
- title screen innerHTML.
- update sound button.
- `this.game = null`? If we null, continue save still available. Yes.
- stop AI timers.
- scene.setPlayers(demo players); sync(demo state).

Careful when returning from game to title: scene players replaced; demo state recreated.

Setup:
`openSetup(prefill?)`:
- App mode is-setup (keeps .is-title? Title screen should hide). Use classes `app.classList.remove('is-title'); app.classList.add('is-setup')`? CSS doesn't hide title for is-setup since title only displays `.is-title .title-screen`; base .title-screen display none, so fine. Topbar hidden since only is-game shows. Modal root active. Board visible behind.
- setup state: count from prefill length or 3; setups array of 4 default entries. If prefill, use.
- render setup modal HTML with rows, count tabs, start button, back close.
- Bind inputs: update setup values on input; role tabs; career select; count changes hide rows and update start.
- Start → sound.unlock(); startGame(setups.slice(0,count)).

Default setups:
- P1: name "You", career engineer, isAI false, color 0
- P2: "Ava", chef, true, color 1
- P3: "Leo", designer, true, color 2
- P4: "Mia", engineer, true, color 3

Maybe human player default name "You". In setup, name input editable. Career select options from CAREERS. Role toggles Human/Computer. For AI careers maybe show select. Good.

UI rows:
```
<div class="setup-player" data-i>
 <span class=color-dot style=--pc>
 <input class=name-input value>
 <div class=role-tabs><button data-role=human class=active>...You</button><button data-role=ai>...</button></div>
 <select class=career-select>...
</div>
```
Icons for human: users, bot.

Count tabs 2 3 4.

Start calls `startGame`.

Start game:
```ts
const seed = Date.now();
this.game = MilestoneGame.newGame(setups, seed);
this.lastSetup = setups;
this.scene.stopCelebrate();
this.scene.setPlayers(this.game.state.players);
this.scene.setActivePlayer(0);
this.scene.showDice([3,4]);
this.scene.sync(this.game.state, true);
app.className='app is-game';
closeModal();
this.turnToken++;
this.renderAll(true);
this.save();
this.scheduleTurn(400);
```
`save()`: localStorage set if game && state.phase==='awaitRoll'? Save only at safe points. At start yes. After finishTurn when awaitRoll. On game end clear. If user quits mid-turn, no save update. Good. Continue loads last awaited turn.
- Note save state can have gameOver; skip if over.
- Save also on hidden? Add visibilitychange: if game and phase awaitRoll, save. Fine.

`renderAll`:
- render playerbar, turnbar, dice readout, log, actionbar, inspector maybe.
- For rendering player cards, use state.
- `scene.sync(game.state)` and setActivePlayer(current).
- Update roll button based on `canRoll && human && !busy`.
- For AI: button disabled with "AI TURN" maybe.
- Update log: reversed last 4; need avoid animation every render? Each render rebuilds giving logIn animations. Fine.
- Show current player's lap chapter.

Turn flow with async token:

```ts
private async beginCurrentTurn(delay=0) {
 const token = ++this.turnToken? No, token per turn. 
 await sleep(delay)
 if (this.game !== currentGame) return
 const p = game.current
 this.renderAll()
 if (game.isOver) return endGame()
 if (p.isAI) {
   this.busy=true; this.updateActionbar()
   await sleep(ai.rollDelay())
   if token invalid return
   await this.performRoll()
 } else {
   this.busy=false; update; hint "Tap Roll"
 }
}
```
Need token check after every await. Use a single `this.runId` increment on any new game/restart/title. Capture `const run = this.runId;` in each async flow.

Maybe implement a turn loop:
```ts
private async runTurnAI() {
 const run = this.runId;
 this.busy = true; update
 await wait(700)
 if (!this.isCurrentRun(run)) return
 await this.doRoll(run)
}
```
`doRoll` is used by human click too; check canRoll. It handles pending and completion.

```ts
private async doRoll(): Promise<void> {
 const game = this.game;
 if (!game || !game.canRoll || this.busy) return;
 this.busy = true;
 this.closeInspector();
